{%- comment -%}
  Sends a successful submission on to a thank-you page.

  Shopify's contact form always posts to /contact and returns to the page it
  came from with ?contact_posted=true — the destination is not something the
  form can set. So the hop happens once we are back on the page, inside the
  branch that only renders after a successful post.

  The link is rendered first and the script replaces the location rather than
  assigning it, so the submitted page does not sit in the back-button history.
  If the script is blocked, the link is the fallback, which is why it carries
  real wording rather than "click here".

  {% render 'tba-form-redirect', url: section.settings.redirect_url,
       label: 'Continue to the thank-you page' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if url != blank -%}
  <a class="tba-form-redirect" href="{{ url }}">{{ label | default: 'Continue' }}</a>
  <script>window.location.replace({{ url | json }});</script>
{%- endif -%}
